WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.560
Is the line really a source?

2
00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.900
Add it somewhere new, and watch what the neighbours do.

3
00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:13.390
A factor is sufficient if adding it where it is normally absent produces the

4
00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:14.390
structure.

5
00:00:14.833 --> 00:00:20.533
First, tissue. Alvarado-Mallart's group often grafted quail brain into chick

6
00:00:20.533 --> 00:00:23.933
embryos, since quail cells look different under the microscope.

7
00:00:24.967 --> 00:00:31.367
In 1991, Martínez, Wassef and Alvarado-Mallart moved tissue from just behind the

8
00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:32.567
junction into the forebrain.

9
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.680
Forebrain cells next to the graft turned on Engrailed.

10
00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.100
Later they developed as midbrain.

11
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.720
The junction could instruct its neighbours.

12
00:00:44.833 --> 00:00:45.993
What was the message?

13
00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:52.193
In 1996, Crossley, Martínez and Gail Martin soaked beads in FGF8.

14
00:00:53.033 --> 00:00:56.113
They placed them in the diencephalon, the back of the forebrain.

15
00:00:56.993 --> 00:00:58.353
An extra midbrain formed.

16
00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:04.347
Predict. The real midbrain still has its own isthmus behind it.

17
00:01:04.987 --> 00:01:06.567
Which way will the new midbrain face?

18
00:01:12.567 --> 00:01:14.987
It was built in reverse, a mirror image.

19
00:01:15.987 --> 00:01:19.287
Parts that normally lie nearest the isthmus formed nearest the bead.

20
00:01:20.317 --> 00:01:22.797
One source is enough to reverse the order.

21
00:01:23.677 --> 00:01:28.717
Here is a toy model, with made-up numbers, with a second source behind it: the bead

22
00:01:28.717 --> 00:01:31.137
and the real isthmus send out the same signal.

23
00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.120
A cell cannot tell which source a molecule came from.

24
00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:41.020
It gets the sum. The sum falls from the bead to the midpoint, then rises toward the

25
00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:42.020
real isthmus.

26
00:01:42.733 --> 00:01:47.553
In a normal midbrain, cells near the isthmus get the most signal, and they build the

27
00:01:47.553 --> 00:01:50.793
back parts. Cells next to the bead get a lot too.

28
00:01:51.653 --> 00:01:53.213
So they build back parts as well.

29
00:01:54.167 --> 00:01:58.707
Farther from the bead, the signal falls, so the parts run toward front of midbrain.

30
00:01:59.827 --> 00:02:03.007
Between the bead and the midpoint, the order runs the wrong way round.

31
00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:12.680
One caution. The tissue around the bead switched on Engrailed-2, and in later bead

32
00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:15.640
experiments its own FGF8 and Wnt1.

33
00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:20.040
That induced organizer probably helped pattern the midbrain too.

34
00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:26.113
Predict. In the 1996 experiment, the bead made midbrain.

35
00:02:27.053 --> 00:02:31.013
But FGF8 normally comes from the side that builds cerebellum.

36
00:02:31.813 --> 00:02:32.813
Why midbrain?

37
00:02:38.467 --> 00:02:43.287
The diencephalon is forebrain, so its cells carry Otx2 and can respond.

38
00:02:44.227 --> 00:02:46.307
At this dose, the response was midbrain.

39
00:02:47.247 --> 00:02:51.647
Whether the response is midbrain or cerebellum also depends on the strength and

40
00:02:51.647 --> 00:02:53.427
duration of FGF8.

41
00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.980
With a strong or lasting source, the rule bends.

42
00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:03.400
In later bead experiments, FGF8 switched Otx2 off and Gbx2 on.

43
00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:06.580
Then isthmus and cerebellum-like tissue formed.

44
00:03:07.583 --> 00:03:09.443
Takeaway: the line is a source.

45
00:03:10.363 --> 00:03:11.883
The signal tells a cell which part.

46
00:03:12.723 --> 00:03:14.923
The repressor sets which region it can become.
